===Fears of Russian involvement===
In October 2017, the Security Committee of the Finnish Ministry of Defence released an assessment on the possibilities of Russian involvement in the presidential election. The assessment addressed nine possible scenarios, ranging from spreading false information through social media to a political assassination. The Security Committee also suggested ten possible objectives for Russian involvement, including obstructing discussion on [[NATO]] and isolating Finland from the [[European Union]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hs.fi/politiikka/art-2000005426871.html |title=Suomi varautuu Venäjän yrityksiin sotkea presidentinvaaleja – puolueet kutsuttiin turvallisuuskokoukseen |work=Helsingin Sanomat|date=28 October 2017 |access-date=29 October 2017 |language=fi}}</ref>

Long-time minister for foreign affairs [[Erkki Tuomioja]] heavily criticised the assessment and called it "pure fantasy resembling something from the pen of [[Ilkka Remes]]".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.is.fi/kotimaa/art-2000005430335.html |title=Tuomioja lyttää turvallisuuskomitean Venäjä-paperin – haukkuu tekijät "pahauskoisiksi hölmöiksi" |work=Ilta-Sanomat|date=31 October 2017 |access-date=31 October 2017 |language=fi}}</ref>

